---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do my guests need an account or an app?', a: 'No. Guests open your wedding link, enter their household code and respond in their browser. There is no app to download or account to create.' },
  { q: 'Can we make the invitation feel like us?', a: 'Yes. Classic and Gala are both included in the free Ivory plan. Choose your colours, photographs and wording, and personalise the details of your celebrations.' },
  { q: 'Can different guests be invited to different events?', a: 'Yes. Organise invitations by person and event. Each household sees the celebrations its members are invited to, and can respond for each person separately.' },
  { q: 'What can we do for free?', a: 'Ivory includes your invitation, events, guest list, RSVPs, import and co-hosts for up to 100 guests. You can begin before choosing a paid plan.' },
  { q: 'How do paid plans work?', a: 'Gold is A$79 once per wedding, with up to 500 guests, budget, checklist and registry. Crimson is A$149 once per wedding, adding vendor tools and room for 1,000 guests. If you already have Gold, the move to Crimson is A$70.' },
  { q: 'Can someone help us organise the wedding?', a: 'Yes. Invite co-hosts to your wedding workspace and choose the access they need. Co-hosts are included with Ivory, Gold and Crimson.' },
  { q: 'How is our guest information used?', a: 'Guest information is used to provide your wedding experience. Your guest list is not public, and guests access their household details with a code. Read our Privacy Notice for how information is handled.' },
]
---
<section id="faq" class="faq-section section-wrap section-space" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="faq-intro" data-reveal><h2 id="faq-heading" class="display">A few things<br />you might be wondering.</h2><p>For your day, and the people in it.</p><a href="/privacy" class="text-link">Our privacy promise <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  <div class="faq-list" data-reveal>{faqs.map(faq => <details><summary>{faq.q}<span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{faq.a}</p></details>)}</div>
</section>
